  "narrative": "Ganymede Industrial has completely stopped buying Diagnostic Equipment for a full 12 months, and this single category loss explains nearly all of the account's 15.3% revenue decline. Three specific products vanished together in September 2025 with zero recovery since, which rules out a seasonal dip. This is a structural loss of a product line, not normal drift, and is dragging high-tier mix down with it.",
  "attributed_categories": [
    "Diagnostic Equipment"
  ],
  "cited_evidence": [
    "Diagnostic Equipment revenue fell from about \u20b935,578 a month to zero and has stayed at zero for 12 straight months since September 2025.",
    "Three Diagnostic Equipment products - the Digital Multimeter Pro, Insulation Tester and Thermal Imager - disappeared entirely with no replacement purchases.",
    "Overall account revenue is down 15.3%, from a baseline of \u20b9202,305 to \u20b9171,462 a month, almost matching the size of the lost category.",
    "High-tier product share fell 5.7 points, from 49.1% to 43.4%, consistent with losing this entirely high-value category.",
    "Margin slipped a smaller 1.6 points, from 28.4% to 26.8%, and discounting and order patterns stayed stable."
  ],
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Contact the account to find out why Diagnostic Equipment purchases stopped entirely in September 2025.",
    "Check whether the customer switched to a competitor or an internal substitute for these three products.",
    "Offer a targeted re-engagement or re-quote on the Digital Multimeter Pro and Insulation Tester lines."
  ],
